x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic extensions of some functions from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $5\\text{th}$ Fourier cosine coefficient of $-3f(x)-2g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $-3f(x)-2g(x)$ are\n\n- $-3{a}_{0}-2{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $-3{a}_{n}-2{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $-3{b}_{n}-2{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $5$th cosine coefficient of $-3f(x)-2g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{5}-2{c}_{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229173 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb295d6c-62fe-59bc-a139-49785ac98f1f" :knowledge-point/title "Using Linearity of Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00485c3e-bd14-5f3f-9feb-953a2cffcf4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{a}_{6}+2{c}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311964} {:answer/id #uuid "297e7733-5db9-565b-9921-843327fd6c18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{b}_{6}+2{d}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312289} {:answer/id #uuid "b96179fa-d64c-5e09-9765-453fcf3d49e0" :answer/