}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $5f(x)+2g(x)$ are\n\n- $5{a}_{0}+2{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $5{a}_{n}+2{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $5{b}_{n}+2{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $6$th cosine coefficient of $5f(x)+2g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n5{a}_{6}+2{c}_{6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30ca427-3074-56c3-828a-1327d7b172b0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of Vertical Shifting and Horizontal Reflection on Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66c5f0e5-aa09-54fe-a222-b89eac0c08dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{a}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312784} {:answer/id #uuid "78af4cb7-64bc-5c86-ab4e-9ee66e85e78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{b}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312935} {:answer/id #uuid "b86ff818-4ce0-5570-acec-52dce6254003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{b}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313408} {:answer/id #uuid "cea22a04-4e37-519a-8d2b-7b7bacd0a32a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313590} {:answer/id #uuid "e821ad92-3013-500e-a5a5-f2d75e298afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{6}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cea22a04-4e37-519a-8d2b-7b7bacd0a32a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313590} :answer-field/id #uuid "79860d23-32c1-578f-b224-5b5b7b31191d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbf29f66-74de-5a85-98a1-53dba6ce09ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-340783" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of a function from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $6$th cosine Fourier coefficient of $f(-x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nRecall that the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(-x)$ are\n\n- ${a}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ${a}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $-{b}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $6$th cosine coefficient of $f(-x)$ is ${a}_{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30ca427-3074-56c3-828a-1327d7b172b0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of Vertical Shifting and Horizontal Reflection on Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24cbc42a-afec-5d14-b112-1b11ca912f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{b}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312250} {:answer/id #uuid "3c8b30e1-f2a6-5f7d-827d-e8490138ab4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186