fficients.\n\nTherefore, the Fourier constant coefficient of $f(-x)$ is ${a}_{0}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "358d4483-c6c6-58cf-b817-eb3410fe7b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312406} {:answer/id #uuid "98837538-4b25-5205-92ff-5cd456e2c2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313183} {:answer/id #uuid "bb45206c-2d2a-5f69-b62d-fc0e1fe41094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98837538-4b25-5205-92ff-5cd456e2c2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313183} :answer-field/id #uuid "2655572b-c1f6-50df-8421-2a489e4a7a37" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "073c65ef-6963-5df0-9c46-0a98e07bba20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312022} {:answer/id #uuid "8526fd82-a0ee-52f2-bcf7-e6914c0f4417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313045} {:answer/id #uuid "9b7734b7-10e8-5a7e-9b49-5338dad6cfcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b7734b7-10e8-5a7e-9b49-5338dad6cfcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313205} :answer-field/id #uuid "484faf9f-2bfa-557e-bbef-c52e5c0a7a18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71628329-43bb-5e3e-a2ae-9baba3c15766" :question/math-academy-id "q-340797" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-{x}^{2}$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the {{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To check whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x)-(-x)^{2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-{x}^{2} \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=f(x),$ we have that $f$ is even.\n\nFor the Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is even and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd, so $f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${b}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{even}$ and the $\\text{sine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01f1f01f-edf5-583a-939f-94b3051cfa20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311974} {:answer/id #uuid "87c00d66-758c-586c-802f-6696e0e6f1ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313059} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b3aaf2-2131-5be5-a3bd-21bf5b6bd924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87c00d66-758c-586c-802f-6696e0e6f1ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313059} :answer-field/id #uuid "08229bd6-8580-5d1e-ad01-ac30abbc7ceb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314036} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "060f67d9-fb05-55e3-b761-fc4cdd697973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312016} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf00aa1-a71e-5073-a380-a99792a18c07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312719} {:answer/id #uuid "66c70bff-83c8-5ce8-87ed-177df75a7d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "060f67d9-fb05-55e3-b761-fc4cdd697973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312016} :answer-field/id #uuid "47222a6b-1c8a-5d58-b0db-1478b882944e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a23b6b8d-69e5-5d60-9ec7-32ca455aba4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340798" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={sin}^{2}⁡(x)+5$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the {{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To check whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & ={sin}^{2}⁡(-x)+5 \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))^{2}+5 \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡(x)+5 \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=f(x),$ we have that $f$ is even.\n\nFor the Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is even and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd, so $f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${b}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{even}$ and the $\\text{sine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6fb8e02-c2ed-54c2-a769-c0f5e618e887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397483} {:answer/id #uuid "82f2576e-7f7d-514c-b7d3-b07f1e9d3631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82f2576e-7f7d-514c-b7d3-b07f1e9d3631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397484} :answer-field/id #uuid "35a58589-56cd-5637-b523-03f859fac5b6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d21a9d-340e-5cb4-a005-7da885a8f606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397486} {:answer/id #uuid "1b091b7e-9971-5f89-be72-b0882bfa2d62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b091b7e-9971-5f89-be72-b0882bfa2d62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397487} :answer-field/id #uuid "52a06cf5-506a-5aec-8bcd-ea5d4fda8897" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8afd30f6-9418-5f9f-a8dd-bdb05d34a03e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340806" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the \n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero."}]}
